  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 314 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe frontal boundary will remain across the forecast area on \nFriday. ATTM, there are differences in the location of this \nfeature with respect to model choice. The NAM soln drops this \nboundary into southern Nebraska, while the GFS has this front \nover the northern third of the forecast area. Like Thursday, \nhigh temperatures will vary widely across the FA and will be \nhighly dependent on frontal position. Based on a compromise in \nfrontal position-ie. EC soln, utilized the NBM for highs Friday \nwhich takes a middle of the road approach with respect to temps \nFriday. The upper level low will accelerate east Friday into \nSaturday, reaching eastern Wyoming by Sunday morning. Shortwaves\nin advance of this feature will lead to a threat for showers \nand thunderstorms Friday, Saturday and Sunday. ATTM, the \ngreatest threat for precipitation appears to be Saturday night \ninto Sunday morning. Beyond Sunday, a second trough of low \npressure will track from the SW CONUS into the intermountain \nwest early next week. This will bring a minor threat for \nprecipitation Monday through Wednesday across the area.",
